This looks like the start of a comment describing what a lock (mutex/spinlock) protects in code. A typical completion would be:

```c
/* This lock protects the shared data structure below. */
```

Common variations you'd see in real codebases:

```c
/* This lock protects all fields in this struct. */
/* This lock protects the device state. */
/* This lock protects access to the global list. */
```

